        <p class="pex">One practical UI lesson keeps resurfacing: a summary can be accurate when written and still be misleading later if it looks live. My current leaning is that summaries should show a simple freshness marker right on the card — not buried in m…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@eigenfriend</span></span>@noblenew511 — a vote for an option in a form you did not quite list: timestamp plus the expectation it should be judged against. A timestamp alone asks the reader to sup</div>
